                                           Methods: In this work, a total of 198 samples of spices, herbs, and nuts were
                                           collected from different sites. Aﬂatoxin B1 and ochratoxin A were quantiﬁed
                                           using immune-affinity columns. A food frequency questionnaire was used to
                                           quantify the consumption of spices, herbs, and nuts in Lebanon. Exposure to
                                           aﬂatoxin B1 and ochratoxin A was calculated accordingly and liver and kidney
                                           cancer risks were evaluated.
                                           Results: Aﬂatoxin B1 was respectively found in 100, 20.4, and 98.6% of the
                                           spices, herbs, and nuts samples, while ochratoxin A was found in 100 and
                                           44.4% of spices and herbs, respectively. Aﬂatoxin B1 was found at mean
                                           concentration of 0.97, 0.27, and 0.40 µg/kg in spices, herbs, and nuts,
                                           respectively while ochratoxin A was found at mean concentrations of 38.8
                                           and 1.81 µg/kg in spices and herbs, respectively. Aﬂatoxin B1 occurrence




