                                                100 ng/kg bw which indicates low risk of renal damage from spices and
                                                herbs consumption.
                                                Conclusion: The consumption of spices, herbs, and nuts in Lebanon could
                                                lead to an increase in health risks associated with aﬂatoxin B1 and ochratoxin
                                                A, speciﬁcally spices. The reported occurrence may be directly related to poor
                                                storage conditions.

