                                  Product selection
                                  The general types of products sampled were selected following a series of global desk assessments that reviewed
                                  literature on lead concentrations in a variety of products in ­LMICs14–17. An initial list of product types and a
                                  sample desk assessment were then provided to the researchers in the countries. The initial list was designed to
                                  examine common items across geographies, but also allowed for flexibility based on local contexts. The research-
                                  ers chose any relevant items for their countries, supporting their point with references (both published and
                                  unpublished), and carried out initial product screening. Based on this formative research, eleven product types
                                  were selected for analysis: ceramic foodware, metal foodware, plastic foodware, cosmetics, toys, paints intended
                                  for large surfaces, paints for art and crafts, spices, sweets, staple dry foods, and traditional and herbal medicines.

