                                                 ble water. Of the 34 water samples tested most lead levels were below the limit of detection and
                                                 7 (21%) were above the US EPA water action level of 15 ppb ranging from 130 to 474 ppb). All
                                                 7 water samples with lead levels exceeding the US EPA water action level were drawn from
                                                 boreholes; 2 were in the Proximal area and 5 were in the Distal area. (Data not shown).

